  "findings": [
    "README describes bibliographic entity resolution and reversible linking/merging, not exact file/image deduplication. No direct algorithm adoption for byte equality.",
    "Six pinned whole files read and verified against canonical git blob IDs. tests/match_test.py contains only commented-out code: zero executable test definitions; path-name inventory must not be treated as test coverage.",
    "match() computes field similarities, applies duplicate rules with non-duplicate exclusions, emits duplicate/maybe labels. Thresholds express bibliographic policy and do not prove byte equality or universal zero false positives advertised by README.",
    "Public merge() recomputes prep/block/match whenever duplicate_id_sets is falsy, including explicitly empty list or empty clustering output. Source observation only; no pandas/runtime control executed.",
    "Example downloader writes response directly without raise_for_status, timeout or atomic replacement; local nonempty/partial cache existence bypasses download. Source only; downloader never invoked.",
    "Other source, preprocessing, blocking, clustering, full tests and datasets remain pending. Full upstream package tests not executed.",
    "Nine further whole files read: cluster, maybe review import/export, blocking, merge, pyproject and four test/fixture sources. Total15/63,48remain.",
    "Five original DFS-body controls reproduce transitive distinct-set chain grouping, same-set split, reversed traversal changing retained pair, empty-set uniqueness exemption and RecursionError for1050nodes at interpreter limit1000. Plain adjacency adapter, not pandas get_connected_components/full package tests.",
    "Source-set uniqueness is documented domain policy. It is not appropriate as a universal exact-file grouping constraint. Transitive bibliographic similarities also do not prove all pairs byte-identical.",
    "Six isolated original merge helper observations: leading empty string loses sole valid title/author/container-title/pages, reversing input retains valid value; two valid titles followed by empty string raisesIndexError; origin union positive control succeeds. pd.isnull adapter limited to None/string fixtures; DataFrame merge not executed.",
    "Blocking groups by hash(tuple(fields)) without raw-key verification at candidate generation; collision could introduce extra candidates, but subsequent matching remains and no final false merge inferred. Candidate combinations materialize quadratically in common blocks; cpu other than1 creates multiprocessing.Pool without specified process count. Source observations, no benchmark.",
    "reduce_distinct_sets excludes same nonempty search_set pairs intentionally; titles with null values are dropped after warning. Domain recall constraints, no universal coverage claim.",
    "Maybe export returns early on empty current cases before touching prior maybe_cases.csv; import reads fixed path without run/dataset binding and removes all remaining maybe labels. Stale review file risk is source-only, no file import/export invoked.",
    "Conditions test queries an empty DataFrame and checks parsing only. Merge test uses two fully populated records and does not cover empty fields. Case test writes EXPORT.csv, so it was not executed in project root. Full upstream tests remain unexecuted."
